d as authorized."}],"span":"I-4","topic":"Unreadable or unverifiable plates"},{"id":"D-6","readings":[{"behaviour":0,"sketch":1,"summary":"Classify dedicated parking as unused only when the holder neither released it nor had a registered vehicle detected entering."},{"behaviour":0,"sketch":3,"summary":"Classify an unreleased dedicated allocation as unused when no registered vehicle was detected entering."}],"span":"I-5","topic":"Dedicated allocation utilization when holder releases parking"}],"round":1,"sketches":[{"spans":[{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"When an employee signs in with an authorized Folio3 Google Workspace account, authenticate the employee using their corporate email address and open their parking-app account."},{"kind":"error","text":"When a personal Gmail account, another email provider, or an account not authorized as a Folio3 employee attempts to sign in, deny access and do not create an employee session."},{"kind":"data","text":"For an employee with dedicated parking, populate or maintain the employee profile from the available employee and parking records, including employee ID, name, parking assignment/status, assigned floor, and registered vehicle details."},{"kind":"data","text":"For a dedicated parking holder with multiple registered vehicles, show and retain the multiple vehicle records associated with that employee."},{"kind":"happy","text":"On a first login by an employee without dedicated parking who has no registered vehicle, prompt them to register at least one license plate before completing their vehicle profile; accept make, model, and color as optional vehicle details."},{"kind":"data","text":"Save a newly entered license plate and any optional vehicle details to the employee's profile for future use."},{"kind":"happy","text":"After successful authentication, take a returning user with a completed profile to the dashboard; direct a first-time user with a missing required vehicle profile to vehicle registration."}],"id":"I