ng."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Show eligible employees the current number of available spaces and let them claim an available space without selecting a specific space."},{"kind":"data","text":"On a successful claim, atomically assign one available space on a first-come, first-served basis, show the assigned parking floor, and record the date, time, employee, and assigned parking."},{"kind":"error","text":"If no space is available when an employee tries to claim, report that none is available and do not create an allocation."},{"kind":"error","text":"If another employee claims the last available space before the request succeeds, reject the later claim and show the refreshed availability rather than assigning the same space twice."},{"kind":"permission","text":"Reject claims by employees with dedicated parking; only employees without dedicated parking can claim temporary availability."},{"kind":"data","text":"Do not treat assignment to a floor as proof that the employee parked there or block the employee based on whether they used the assigned floor."}],"id":"I-3","readingChosen":"First-come, first-served means the first successful claim of an available allocation wins; a claim is for an automatically assigned space/floor rather than a user-selected space."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"At the entrance, detect approaching cars and read their license plates; ignore pedestrians, motorcycles, and other non-car objects."},{"kind":"happy","text":"For a vehicle without a permanent parking sticker, check the detected plate against valid temporary parking allocations for the current day."},{"kind":"happy","text":"When a matching current-day temporary authorization exists, activate the green indicator so the security guard can allow entry."},{"kind":"error","text":"When no valid current-day authorization exists, keep the indicator off and do not authorize entry; the security guard must not allow the vehicle in on the basis of this check."},{"kind":"data","text":"For 