orate email, and retrieve their employee profile from the corporate directory."},{"kind":"permission","text":"Reject personal Gmail accounts, other email providers, and Folio3 accounts that are not authorized employees; do not grant application access."},{"kind":"data","text":"For an employee with dedicated parking, populate and maintain the available employee and parking profile, including employee ID and name, parking status, assigned floor, and registered vehicle details and plate numbers."},{"kind":"happy","text":"For an employee without dedicated parking who has no registered vehicle, prompt them on first login to register at least one license plate; accept make, model, and color as optional vehicle details and save the profile for future use."},{"kind":"error","text":"If the required vehicle registration is incomplete, keep the employee from completing the first-login vehicle-profile step; after successful login and completed profile setup, take returning users to the dashboard."}],"id":"I-1","readingChosen":"Treat “authorized Folio3 Google accounts” as authorized Folio3 employees authenticating through corporate Google Workspace, not any account with a Gmail address."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"permission","text":"Allow only an employee with dedicated parking to release their assigned space for today; a single action releases it and confirms success, and the holder can see whether it is reserved, released, or claimed."},{"kind":"data","text":"On a valid release, record the release for that date and make the space eligible for temporary allocation according to the daily release-time rules."},{"kind":"error","text":"Reject a repeat release of the same space for the same day. If another employee has already claimed it, tell the holder it cannot be reclaimed that day without administrator intervention."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Allow a dedicated parking holder to select one or more future dates within the next 30 days and save the releases for those dates; show saved releases on the calendar."},{"kind":"data","text":"Allow the holder to cancel a scheduled release while it has not been claimed, and record the cancellation in the release audit history."},{"kind":"error","text":"If a requested date is outside the next 30 days, the user is not a dedicated parking holder, or the release has already been claimed, reject the action and explain that it cannot be completed; claimed releases require administrator intervention to revert."}],"id":"I-2","readingChosen":"Treat “schedule releases up to 30 days ahead” as allowing selection of dates within the next 30 days, including multiple dates, and include cancellation only while unclaimed."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"When released spaces become available, send a push notification to eligible employees without dedicated parking and show the current number of available spaces in the app."},{"kind":"data","text":"Make prescheduled releases and same-day releases made before the configured daily release time available at that time (default 8:00 AM); make same-day releases made after that time available immediately."},{"kind":"permission","text":"Allow only employees without dedicated parking to claim an available space; allocate one available space to the first successful claimant, record the claim time, employee, date, and assigned space, and show the assigned parking floor."},{"kind":"error","text":"When no space remains by the time an employee attempts to claim, do not allocate a space and show that no space is available; each released space can be claimed only once."},{"kind":"data","text":"Do not require the temporary parking user to choose a specific space or verify that they park on the assigned floor."}],"id":"I-3","readingChosen":"Interpret first-come, first-served as allocation to the first successful claim request; a release is claimable only at its applicable availability time."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"For an approaching car without a permanent parkin